class:: FMMatrixExp
summary:: Exponential frequency-modulation matrix with octave-valued depths
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/FMMatrixUGens, Classes/FMMatrix, Classes/PMMatrix

description::
Extends the independent FM7-inspired matrix architecture with exponential FM: code::effectiveFreq[i] = freqs[i] * 2.pow(sum(M[i][j] * previous[j]))::. Rows are destinations and columns are sources. Output is amplitude times the sine of the double-precision carrier phase; that phase advances using effective frequency after output. Every edge reads the complete preceding network state, preserving one host sample of delay at all oversampling factors.

Negative base frequencies remain negative and a zero base stays zero. For numerical safety, the summed octave exponent is bounded to -128 through +128 before exponentiation. This is an implementation bound, not a suggested musical range. Modulation can shift average pitch and generate aliased sidebands. Dense cost grows as code::oversample * N.squared::. Initial feedback/filter state is zero.

This resembles driving link::Classes/SinOsc:: frequency with an octave-to-ratio conversion, but adds an internal synchronous network. Unlike link::Classes/FMMatrix::, depths represent octaves, not Hz; unlike link::Classes/PMMatrix::, they do not directly offset output phase.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freqs
Scalar or per-operator base frequencies in Hz; size fixes operator count. Signed and audio-rate values are supported.

argument:: phases
Scalar or per-operator initial radians, sampled at construction.

argument:: amps
Scalar or per-operator amplitude, affecting output and internal modulation.

argument:: modMatrix
Exact NxN matrix in octaves per unit source amplitude, default zero. Divide semitone depths by 12. Control entries ramp over one block; audio entries are read per sample.

argument:: resetTrig
Scalar or per-operator nonpositive-to-positive phase-reset trigger. Feedback history is retained.

argument:: resetPhase
Scalar or per-operator reset radians, read on trigger edges.

argument:: oversample
Constant 1, 2, 4 or 8. FIR decimation adds 0, 15.5, 23.25 or 27.125 host samples of latency. Interpolation and filtering follow the project guide; alias reduction is patch-dependent.

argument:: smooth
Additional matrix-only one-pole time in seconds, scalar/control-rate. Zero disables extra lag; positive times mean a 63.2 percent response and also affect audio-rate depths.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier with standard multichannel behavior.

argument:: add
Output offset with standard multichannel behavior.

returns::
An Array of raw operator outputs.

examples::
code::
(

    // 2-operator exponential FM with constant depth
    x = {
        var ops = FMMatrixExp.ar([110, 73], 0, [1, 0.7], [[0, 0.8], [0, 0]], oversample: 2);
        (ops[0] * 0.12 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)) ! 2
    }.play;
)
::


code::
(

    // Deep exponential FM droning
    x = {
        var modMatrix = [
            [SinOsc.kr(0.1).range(0, 0.5), 1.2],
            [0.5, SinOsc.kr(0.15).range(0, 0.3)]
        ];
        var ops = FMMatrixExp.ar([55, 110], 0, [1, 1], modMatrix, oversample: 2);
        (ops[0] * 0.15 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.5)) ! 2
    }.play;
)
::

code::
(

    // Cross-modulated exponential bells
    x = {
        var env = EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.01, 2), Dust.kr(1));
        var modMatrix = [
            [0, env * 2],
            [env * 1.5, 0]
        ];
        var ops = FMMatrixExp.ar([440, 880], 0, [1, 0.5], modMatrix, oversample: 4);
        (ops[0] * 0.15 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)) ! 2
    }.play;
)
::
